\viewkind4\uc1\pard\fi-225\li225\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. \cf0  When I survey the wondrous cross
\par \pard\li225\sl190\slmult0  On which the Prince of Glory died,
\par  My riches gain I count but loss,
\par  And pour contempt on all my pride.
\par 
\par \pard\fi-225\li225\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2.  Forbid it, Lord, that I should boast,
\par \pard\li225\sl190\slmult0\qj  Save in the death of Christ, my God;
\par  All the vain things that charm me most,
\par  I sacrifice them to his blood.
\par \pard\li225\sl190\slmult0 
\par \pard\fi-225\li315\sl190\slmult0\qj\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. See! From his head, his hands, his feet,
\par \pard\li315\sl190\slmult0 Sorrow and love flow mingled down;
\par Did e'er such love and sorrow meet,
\par Or thorns compose so rich a crown?
\par 
\par \pard\fi-225\li315\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. Were the whole realm of nature mine,
\par \pard\li315\sl190\slmult0 That were an offering far too small;
\par Love so amazing, so divine,
\par \pard       Demands my soul, my life, my all.\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b\f2 
\par }

